    "entrance": "Low western shelf beneath an outgoing rail.",
    "exit": "Long eastern landing beyond the rail stop, under its thorned overhang.",
    "solution": "Catch the outward rail and release toward the paired pod and low bell. A downward cut without Jump makes a low rebound beneath the roof and rings the bell: the transfer shutter disappears and the blue middle landing appears. Land there, jump into the vertical carriage, and reel up. Its upper bell is reachable from the moving rope. Cut it as you prepare to leave: the blue landing below disappears and the gold exit bridge becomes solid. Jump-release onto that bridge. The floor that lets you catch the lift and the floor that lets you leave it cannot exist together.",
    "nearestExisting": "The previous B41 only asked for a low rebound after an optional rail ride. F39 uses an echo-held stop for a train transfer. This version makes the selected rebound exchange the actual landing state, and the second moving anchor lets the knight give up that landing in midair to create the exit.",
    "novelty": "Two phase changes have opposing jobs: the first removes a shutter and supplies the boarding station; the second consumes that station to create the upper exit. The moving lift is the place to survive between those mutually exclusive floor layouts.",
