    "designNotes": "The original broad end shelf is replaced with two mutually exclusive phase supports and a vertical transfer. The first shutter blocks the direct swing route beneath the immovable roof. No receipts or event-conditioned exits are used: bells change the same visible A/B solids. A stopped first rail cannot carry the player to the exit. All movement is ordinary rope control and controlled low pogo; no dash.",
    "revision": {
      "date": "2026-10-09",
      "archive": "scripts/room-bank/archive/run4-before-superrooms/base/bank-b41.json",
      "latestChanges": "Rebuilt the single departure as a low bell/rebound into a phase landing, then a vertical carrier departure that consumes that landing to create the exit."
    },
    "userFeedback": {
      "date": "2026-10-09",
      "comment": "Direct ramp swing skips first pogo, and ramp into pogo is too simple. Make the puzzle harder and more complex."
    }
